WEBVTT

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:02.707 line:86%
Your client sent you a specific

00:00:02.747 --> 00:00:04.820 line:86%
armchair to add to the project, but

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.900 line:86%
you couldn't find it in the 3D

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:07.640 line:86%
Warehouse?

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.990 line:86%
Now it's much easier with Vizai.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.342 line:86%
Just take an image from

00:00:11.382 --> 00:00:13.251 line:86%
the internet or from the supplier

00:00:13.291 --> 00:00:14.273 line:86%
and import it into

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:14.914 line:86%
the plugin,

00:00:14.954 --> 00:00:16.474 line:86%
and it creates a perfect block

00:00:16.514 --> 00:00:17.214 line:86%
for you.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.311 line:86%
Just save the image and upload

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:20.710 line:86%
it inside the plugin.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.768 line:86%
The only thing to worry about

00:00:22.808 --> 00:00:24.680 line:86%
is choosing the polygon level.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:25.904 line:86%
I always keep it on

00:00:25.944 --> 00:00:27.316 line:86%
the recommended mode,

00:00:27.356 --> 00:00:28.892 line:86%
so it doesn't weigh down

00:00:28.932 --> 00:00:30.510 line:86%
your SketchUp file.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.210 line:86%
Once generated,

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.477 line:86%
you get two options:

00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:03.290 line:86%
one to import the block into

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.710 line:86%
the project and another to save

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.861 line:86%
it on your computer.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.209 line:86%
Then just adjust the scale a bit,

00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:10.510 line:86%
in case it comes in a little smaller

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.716 line:86%
or a little larger than the real

00:01:11.756 --> 00:01:12.456 line:86%
thing.

